Data Collection Tools TOOL 0: INFORMED CONSENT FORMS (All Stakeholder Categories) Administration Instructions: Two versions are provided: Written Consent Form (for participants with adequate literacy) and Oral Consent Script (for participants with low literacy or cognitive impairment). Both versions must be translated into all six city languages before deployment. ICSSR Approval No.: ________ (insert before deployment). All consent forms must be pre-tested with a non-researcher native speaker in each city. TOOL 0A: Written Informed Consent Form - Oldest Old Participants Instrument Code CONSENT-OOP-W Instrument Title Written Informed Consent Form - Oldest Old Persons Type Consent Documentation Target Stakeholder Oldest Old Persons (75 - 85 years), community-dwelling and old age home residents Applicable Cities All six cities -language-adapted versions required Session Duration 10 -15 minutes for reading and signing Administration Mode Administered by Field Investigator; participant signs or thumb-prints INFORMED CONSENT FOR PARTICIPATION IN RESEARCH Study Title: Smart Cities, Silent Citizens -The Impact of ‘Digital-by-Default’ Governance on the Autonomy and Well-being of the Oldest Old Population Funding Body: Indian Council of Social Science Research (ICSSR), Major Research Project 2025-26 Principal Investigator: ____________________________ | Institution: ____________________________ ICSSR Approval No.: ______ | Contact for Concerns: ______ | Date: ______ What is this study about? This is an academic research project studying how new digital services introduced in Smart Cities -such as mobile apps/websites to access e-governance portals, QR codes to access basic amenities, online portals, digital kiosks, etc. -affect the daily lives, independence, and well-being of older persons above the age of 75. The research will help policymakers improve city services for older citizens. The study is funded by the Indian Council of Social Science Research (a Government of India body) and has no commercial purpose. What will you be asked to do? • Answer a set of questions about your experiences using (or trying to use) digital services in your city. This takes approximately 45-55 minutes and will happen in one session. • Participate in a longer, more detailed conversation about your daily life in the city. This takes approximately 60-75 minutes and will happen on a different day. • [OPTIONAL] Allow a researcher to accompany you to a public place to observe your interactions with city services there. This is entirely optional and requires separate consent. ICSSR Major Research Project 2025–26 | Smart Cities, Silent Citizens | 3



Data Collection Tools • All participation is entirely voluntary. You may skip any question or stop at any time. Will your answers be kept private? Yes. Your name will never appear on any research document. You will be assigned a participant code number, and only that code will be used in all records. The only document linking your name to your code is kept in a locked file at the researcher’s institution and will be destroyed after the study ends. Your responses will be combined with hundreds of others and reported only as group findings -never individually. Will the conversation be audio-recorded? We would like to audio-record the longer conversation (not the questionnaire) so we can accurately write down what you say. This is optional -you may refuse recording and the interviewer will take written notes instead. Recordings are transcribed and then permanently deleted. What are the risks? The risk is minimal. Some questions ask about personal experiences that may feel emotionally sensitive. You may skip any question or stop at any time without giving a reason. If you are in an old age home, your care will not be affected in any way by your decision to participate or withdraw. Is participation voluntary? Yes. You may withdraw at any time without any consequence to you or your family. If you withdraw, any data you have already provided will not be used. CONSENT DECLARATION I confirm that I have read (or had read to me) the above information. I understand the purpose of this research, what I am being asked to do, how my privacy will be protected, and that I can withdraw at any time. I voluntarily agree to participate in this study. Participant Name (or mark if unable to sign):



