Data Collection Tools TOOL 1: STRUCTURED QUESTIONNAIRE FOR OLDEST OLD PERSONS (SQ-OOP-v1.0) Instrument Code SQ-OOP-v1.0 Instrument Title Structured Questionnaire -Oldest Old Persons in Smart Cities Type Quantitative -Structured Questionnaire with Likert Scales, Frequency Items, Dependency Index, and Dignity Perception Scale Target Stakeholder Oldest Old Persons aged 75- 85 years (community-dwelling and old age home residents) Applicable Cities All six cities: New Delhi, Srinagar, Aizawl, Chennai, Gandhinagar, Indore -city-specific language versions required Session Duration 45-55 minutes. Mandatory break at 25-minute mark. Do NOT exceed 60 minutes total. Administration Mode Read-aloud by Field Investigator in local language. Self-administration is NOT appropriate. Large-print version (16pt+) mandatory. Responses recorded by FI. Administration Instructions: CRITICAL ADMINISTRATION RULES:(1) Conduct in PRIVATE -no family members, caregivers, or institution staff present during the session. (2) Read every question aloud. Show the response option card simultaneously for visual reference.(3) If participant is visually impaired: read all response options aloud slowly; participant responds verbally.(4) If participant shows signs of fatigue, confusion, or distress: PAUSE and offer a break; terminate session if distress persists.(5) NEVER administer both this questionnaire AND the SSI-OOP in the same session -minimum 2-day gap required.(6) Mark skipped items with ‘S’ and note reason in margin.(7) Time-stamp all sessions. Alert at 25-minute mark for mandatory break. Participant ID Date of Interview City Start / End Time Field Investigator Code Location Type Comm.-dwelling / OAH-Govt / OAH-Private / Other Neighbourhood / Ward Break Given at 25 min? YES / NO (this can be skipped) SEC A SOCIO-DEMOGRAPHIC PROFILE Administration Instructions: All items are factual. Record exactly what the participant says. For age verification, note the document type used. Do not estimate or assume age. ICSSR Major Research Project 2025–26 | Smart Cities, Silent Citizens | 8



