Data Collection Tools TOOL 3: EXPERT AND KEY INFORMANT INTERVIEW GUIDES (SSI-MoHUA/SPV, SSI-UP, SSI-ICCC, FI-MCO) TOOL 3A: Expert Interview -MoHUA Officials and Smart City SPV Officers Instrument Code SSI-MoHUA/SPV-v1.0 Instrument Title Semi-Structured Expert Interview -Ministry of Housing and Urban Affairs Officials and Smart City SPV Officers Type Qualitative -Semi-Structured Expert Interview using Elite Interviewing approach Target Stakeholder MoHUA officers (Central); Smart City SPV CEOs, Directors, Programme Managers; State Urban Development Department officials Applicable Cities All six cities + Central Government for MoHUA-level interviews Session Duration 60–90 minutes Administration Mode Audio-recorded with consent. English or Hindi. City-language on request. Administration Instructions: INTERVIEWING GUIDANCE:Provide the one-page research brief and consent form (CONSENT-KI) 10-15 minutes before starting. Use an informed, evidence-based approach -reference specific SCM project examples from the city. Probe politely but persistently when institutional PR responses are given. Triangulate with observation data and documentary evidence in follow-up probes. T1 DESIGN PHILOSOPHY AND STAKEHOLDER CONSULTATION IN SCM PROJECT DEVELOPMENT Opening Question: ‘Could you begin by walking us through how a new Smart City project is conceptualized, designed, and approved in [city / ministry] -from the initial idea through to implementation? I am particularly interested in the key decision points and who holds authority at each stage’. Probing Questions / Follow-ups: 45. At which specific stages of this process are end-users consulted? Who formally represents elderly or differently-abled residents in these consultations? 46. Is there a mandatory checklist or formal criterion related to accessibility or universal design that every project must satisfy before approval? 47. Has the age profile of potential users ever been a formal input into any project's design specifications? Can you give a concrete example from your city? 48. Are you aware of any SCM project in your city that was modified or retrofitted after deployment because elderly users found it inaccessible? What was the trigger for that change? 49. Does your SPV or Ministry have any specific standard operating procedure related to universal design, age-friendly design, or digital accessibility? ICSSR Major Research Project 2025–26 | Smart Cities, Silent Citizens | 25



Data Collection Tools T2 UNDERSTANDING AND DATA ON DIGITAL EXCLUSION IN YOUR SMART CITY From your professional observation over the years, how do elderly residents -particularly those above 75 years of age -interact with the digital services introduced under the Smart Cities Mission in your city? Probing Questions / Follow-ups: 50. Has your office or city ever conducted a formal user survey or needs assessment specifically focused on elderly residents and their digital access? If yes, what did it reveal? 51. Do you receive complaints or grievances from elderly residents about their inability to access digital services? How are those handled institutionally -what is the process? 52. Does your ICCC or any city-level data system capture age-disaggregated usage data for any of your digital services? If yes, would you share that data formally with our research? 53. In your professional assessment, what proportion of your city’s oldest residents -those between 75 and 85 years -can independently and successfully use the key digital services you have deployed? 54. What does ‘digital inclusion’ mean, in practical terms, for a 78-year-old who grew up and worked entirely before computers existed? Is that definition reflected anywhere in how your city currently plans its services? T3 LEGAL AND POLICY FRAMEWORK -CONVERGENCE WITH ELDERLY WELFARE SCM operates alongside several other policy frameworks, including the National Policy for Older Persons 2011, the Maintenance and Welfare of Parents and Senior Citizens Act 2007, and the Atal Vayo Abhyudaya Yojana. How does your city or ministry coordinate with these frameworks in practice? Probing Questions / Follow-ups: 55. Is there any formal convergence mechanism between the Ministry of Housing and Urban Affairs and the Ministry of Social Justice and Empowerment on the specific issue of elderly digital inclusion in smart cities? 56. Are you aware of the constitutional mandate under Article 21 (right to life with dignity) and Article 4