Data Collection Tools 63. Would you be willing to share the following with our research formally? [Note response]: city-level SCM project completion reports, user satisfaction surveys, ICCC dashboard or usage data, age-disaggregated interaction data, design specifications for key completed projects. T5 FORWARD VISION -AGE-CENTRIC REDESIGN AND POLICY REFORM If you were given a specific mandate and adequate resources to redesign your city’s SCM projects with the needs of the oldest old population -those between 75 and 85 -as the primary design criterion, what would change most significantly? Probing Questions / Follow-ups: 64. What institutional, financial, or political barriers currently prevent more age-inclusive design in Smart City projects? 65. Are you aware of any international Smart City model -whether in Europe, East Asia, or elsewhere -that has addressed elderly digital inclusion effectively? What specific lessons do you think are applicable to the Indian context? 66. What single policy change at the central government level -whether a funding condition, a mandatory guideline, or a legislative amendment -would most effectively drive cities toward age-inclusive digital infrastructure design? 67. Would you be willing to review the policy recommendations from this research before publication and provide feedback? [Note response for follow-up] Field Investigator Note: After the interview: Request the following documents if available:[ ] City SCM project completion reports[ ] Any user satisfaction surveys conducted by the SPV[ ] ICCC dashboard reports or annual data summaries[ ] Any age-disaggregated digital service usage data[ ] Design specifications for key completed SCM projects in the city TOOL 3B: Expert Interview -Urban Planners and Interface Designers (SSI-UP) Instrument Code SSI-UP-v1.0 Instrument Title Semi-Structured Expert Interview -Urban Planners, Architects, and UX/Interface Designers Type Qualitative -Expert Interview with Heuristic Design Discussion Target Stakeholder Urban planners and architects engaged in SCM project design; UX or interface designers for SCM digital systems; technology vendor design teams Applicable Cities City-specific -targeted at individuals who designed key SCM physical or digital infrastructure Session Duration 60–75 minutes Administration Mode Audio-recorded with consent. Opening: Please start by telling me about your professional role and which specific SCM projects in [city] you have been involved in designing or implementing. Probing Questions / Follow-ups: 68. What were the stated user requirements when you began designing [project name]? Who defined those requirements? 69. Were there any explicit accessibility standards -Indian or international, such as WCAG or the RPWD Act provisions -that you were required to follow for this project? ICSSR Major Research Project 2025–26 | Smart Cities, Silent Citizens | 27



